<title>JAPAN: Shinagawa Fuel plans to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Shinagawa Fuel plans to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petroleum products maker Shinagawa Fuel Co Ltd said on Friday that it plans to buy back up to 4.5 million of its common shares at a cost not to exceed three billion yen.</p>
<p>The repurchase plan will require formal approval at its shareholders' meeting in late June, the company said.</p>
<p>Shinagawa also said the company will change its name to Sinanen Co Ltd on April 1, 1998.</p>
<p>Shares of Shinagawa closed at 600 yen on Friday.</p>
</text>
